--- TURN 1 ---
Fixed and verified.

**Root cause:** `binary_search` used `while lo < hi`. When the search window collapsed to a single element (`lo == hi`), the loop exited without ever checking `arr[lo]`, so a target at the only remaining position was missed (returned -1). It also meant last-element lookups like `[1,2], 2` broke.

**Fix** (`search.py:7`): changed the loop condition to `while lo <= hi` — standard binary search. Same signature, still O(log n). No changes to `test_search.py`, no new files.

**Verification:** all 7 tests pass (`7 passed in 0.15s`).

Note: system python had no pytest, so I ran it via `uv run --with pytest` — same suite, just an available interpreter.

